parts.part_stem:
The variation with time of the potential difference (p.d.) of the input signal is shown in Fig. 5.2.
{{figure:figure_5_2}}
The ADC has a sampling frequency of $250\text{Hz}$ and uses 4-bit sampling, with the least significant bit corresponding to $1\text{ mV}$. The signal is first sampled at time 0, when the sampled bits are 0001.

parts.text:
Part of the signal received by the receiver, after the sampled signal has passed through the DAC, is shown in Fig. 5.3.
{{figure:figure_5_3}}
On Fig. 5.3, complete the line to show the received signal for time 0 to time $12\text{ms}$.

The ADC in (b) is replaced with one that has a sampling frequency of $500\text{Hz}$ and uses 3-bit sampling, with the least significant bit corresponding to $2\text{ mV}$.
On Fig. 5.4, sketch the signal that is now received, after passing through the DAC, from time 0 to time $12\text{ms}$.
{{figure:figure_5_4}}

